  "finding": {
    "id": "sha256:b5a25922e9ffac968ad649e45fae7b98fa97ad6a252c0da394786819f8f118f4",
    "waveId": "15ee8fd61229d74b3bfc53d90723305e2dec222c8e15c6f814fb82f373d6aa8d",
    "target": "validation/validation.gate/15ee8fd61229d74b3bfc53d90723305e2dec222c8e15c6f814fb82f373d6aa8d:merge-gate",
    "raw": {
      "id": "",
      "digest": "",
      "severity": "P1",
      "severityRationale": "A bound acceptance condition of the merge gate is directly violated, so the gate cannot pass; however the protective core of AC-004 (nonzero exit, no success output on stdout) already works and the defect is a one-line stderr message prefix in frob.go within the already-authorized rework scope — major contract violation requiring rework before merge, but not a total AC failure (exit 0 with success output) that would warrant P0.",
      "requirement": "REQ-001 / AC-004: 传入未知 flag（例如 --unknown-flag）时 frob 以非零退出码拒绝执行，且不输出 frob: 行（此条件归 master-merge）。Issued criterion: unknown flags must exit nonzero and emit no frob: output.",
      "normalPath": "frob --unknown-flag canary rejects execution with a nonzero exit code and emits no line beginning with the reserved 'frob: ' prefix on any stream; rejection diagnostics use a non-reserved wording (the codebase already does this on the insufficient-args path with 'usage: frob <word>'), keeping 'frob: ' an unambiguous marker of the normal success line 'frob: UPPER bytes=N'.",
      "actualError": "frob.go:3 rejects any argument starting with '-' via fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"frob: unknown flag %q\\nusage: frob <word>\\n\", arg) followed by os.Exit(2). The first stderr line therefore begins with 'frob: ', so the program outputs a frob: line during rejection. Confirmed by host observation 'public flag-contract probe': exit 2 with captured output 'frob: unknown flag \"--unknown-flag\"\\nusage: frob <word>'.",
      "deferralImpact": "If merged as-is, every consumer or harness that keys on 'frob: ' lines (grep over combined stdout/stderr, scripts treating any frob: output as a result line) cannot distinguish rejection from success; the public flag contract that AC-004 reserved at master-merge remains broken and downstream users inherit the ambiguity. The fix is a one-line stderr message change in frob.go, already inside this run's authorized rework scope, so deferral buys nothing.",
      "verification": {},
      "message": "AC-004 violated: the unknown-flag rejection emits a line starting with the reserved 'frob: ' prefix. The candidate correctly exits nonzero (2) and leaves stdout empty, but its rejection diagnostic 'frob: unknown flag \"--unknown-flag\"' is itself a 'frob: ' line, so frob does emit frob: output while rejecting an unknown flag. AC-001, AC-002 and AC-003 were independently verified against source and probes and are satisfied; only AC-004 fails.",
      "locations": [
        "/private/tmp/canary-flag-workspace/frob.go:3",
        "/private/tmp/canary-flag-jobs/engine-canary/act_validation_validation.gate_15ee8fd61229d74b3bfc53d90723305e2dec222c8e15c6f814fb82f373d6aa8d_merge-gate/att_validation_validation.gate_15ee8fd61229d74b3bfc53d90723305e2dec222c8e15c6f814fb82f373d6aa8d_merge-gate_58/materials.json (hostObservations[2], public flag-contract probe)"
      ]
    },
    "history": null
  },
